sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as psql runner A
    participant B as psql runner B
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    Note over A,D: Catalog advisory (65102, 2): protects price_versions, not a column
    A->>D: BEGIN, migration advisory lock (65102, 1)
    B->>D: BEGIN, same migration advisory lock
    Note over B,D: WAIT before reading or creating schema_migrations
    A->>D: Read applied versions<br/>Apply missing SQL and insert version records
    alt A completes
        A->>D: COMMIT schema changes and records together
        D-->>B: Migration lock granted
        B->>D: Read committed versions, skip applied migrations
        B->>D: COMMIT without repeating their effects
    else A fails
        A->>D: ROLLBACK schema changes and version records
        D-->>B: Migration lock granted
        B->>D: Read versions, apply missing migrations<br/>Store their records, COMMIT
    end
    Note over A,D: Connection termination also releases transaction locks.<br/>Migration key 1 differs from catalog key 2.<br/>DDL still takes normal PostgreSQL relation locks.<br/>This runner lock does not promise online migrations.
